dcomp: print the bridge's gate and registration diagnostics when they change, not every 2 seconds

What was seen: a user's bug report (GitHub Neutron#49) carried 150 log lines that were nothing but
"neutron-gate: 2s window calls=... (gate ...)" and "neutron-reg: N live registrations", one pair every
2 seconds for the whole session, burying the lines that mattered.

Mechanism: dcomp's bridge thread (presentations_proc) keeps two lab diagnostics from the M4 work: the
present gate's 2 s statistics (blit_swapchain_to_hwnd) and the live registration count. Both printed at ERR
level on every 2 s window, whether or not anything had changed.

Change: the same 2 s cadence and the same line format, but a line is printed for the first window and then
only when what it reports changes: the gate line when its state flips between ENGAGED and not-skipping,
the registration line when the live count changes. Lab harnesses that grep these lines still see every
state (none counts them per time: checked our test harnesses and the lab
tools; one counts "neutron-gate" but never reports that count). A stalled bridge thread is
still reported by neutron-blit-slow (capcut-locks), which this does not touch.

Windows behavior: not applicable (diagnostic only; no behavior change).

Not covered: the other periodic neutron-* lines in the same report (dcomp-hook PresentBase is once per
swap chain since dxvk-dxgi 0004; the winewayland ownedsub repeats are cjk48's patch).

Lab evidence (lab runtime 11.10-186rc, CapCut start + 120 s on a nested desk, capcut-locks' start1.sh, WINEDEBUG=+timestamp):
  11.10-185:   neutron-gate 116 / neutron-reg 116 lines in ~123 s (56 per minute each), 3 of 4 runs; 61 / 56 in the
               run where the bridge thread stalled.
  11.10-186rc: neutron-gate 2 / neutron-reg 3 lines (the first line in each of CapCut's two bridge processes, plus one
               registration count change), 2 of 2 runs.
  11.10-186rc + NEUTRON_DCOMP_DIAG_PERIODIC=1: 116 / 116 lines and "neutron-gateresolved: NEUTRON_DCOMP_DIAG_PERIODIC = 1"
               in both processes (1 run).

Kill switch: NEUTRON_DCOMP_DIAG_PERIODIC=1 prints both lines every 2 s again (as 11.10-185).

--- a/dlls/dcomp/device.c	2026-11-09 09:39:05.831722812 -0500
+++ b/dlls/dcomp/device.c	2026-11-09 09:39:53.124100012 -0500
@@ -296,6 +296,23 @@
  * tick again (the old coupling). */
 static CRITICAL_SECTION blit_cs;
 
+/* NEUTRON (Neutron#49): the bridge's two periodic diagnostics ("neutron-gate: 2s window ..." and "neutron-reg: N live
+ * registrations") are printed for the first 2 s window and then only when what they report changes (the gate's state
+ * flips between ENGAGED and not-skipping, the live registration count changes); a user's log carried 150 lines of
+ * nothing else. Same 2 s cadence, same line format, so harnesses that grep them still see every state.
+ * NEUTRON_DCOMP_DIAG_PERIODIC=1 prints them every 2 s again. */
+static int neutron_dcomp_diag_periodic(void)
+{
+    static int v = -1;
+    if (v < 0)
+    {
+        char b[8];
+        v = (GetEnvironmentVariableA("NEUTRON_DCOMP_DIAG_PERIODIC", b, sizeof(b)) && b[0] == '1') ? 1 : 0;
+        if (v) ERR("neutron-gateresolved: NEUTRON_DCOMP_DIAG_PERIODIC = 1\n");
+    }
+    return v;
+}
+
 static int neutron_blit_unlocked(void)
 {
     static int v = -1;
@@ -746,9 +763,13 @@
             if (g_t == 0) g_t = now;
             if (now - g_t >= 2000)
             {
+                static int g_last = -1;   /* gate state last printed: -1 none yet, 0 not-skipping, 1 ENGAGED */
+                int state = g_skips > 0;
                 g_t = now;
-                ERR("neutron-gate: 2s window calls=%ld blits=%ld skips=%ld (gate %s)\n",
-                    c, g_blits, g_skips, g_skips > 0 ? "ENGAGED" : "not-skipping");
+                if (state != g_last || neutron_dcomp_diag_periodic())
+                    ERR("neutron-gate: 2s window calls=%ld blits=%ld skips=%ld (gate %s)\n",
+                        c, g_blits, g_skips, state ? "ENGAGED" : "not-skipping");
+                g_last = state;
                 InterlockedExchange(&g_calls, 0); InterlockedExchange(&g_blits, 0); InterlockedExchange(&g_skips, 0);
             }
         }
@@ -1328,7 +1349,14 @@
          * plateau at the true live-window count (~15-25), never climb into the thousands. */
         now = GetTickCount64();
         if (regt == 0) regt = now;
-        if (now - regt >= 2000) { regt = now; ERR("neutron-reg: %d live registrations\n", nlive); }
+        if (now - regt >= 2000)
+        {
+            static int reg_last = -1;   /* count last printed, -1 none yet */
+            regt = now;
+            if (nlive != reg_last || neutron_dcomp_diag_periodic())
+                ERR("neutron-reg: %d live registrations\n", nlive);
+            reg_last = nlive;
+        }
         /* NEUTRON round-34 ztree diag: dump the real win32 z-order every ~5s */
         if (neutron_ztree_diag())
         {
